=== FILE @workspace/CLAUDE.md (644) ===
# Golden workspace

The Trustworks Essentials project lives at **`./golden/`**. All implementation work — source files, tests, configurations, frontend assets, build scripts — belongs inside that subdirectory. Do **not** create new source files at this workspace root.

When using any planner/implementer tooling at this workspace level: either `cd golden/` first, or scope every file path in design/implementation specs with the `golden/` prefix. A "Greenfield. All paths are new" design that omits this prefix is a contradiction with the existing scaffold and must be corrected, not followed literally.

## Project pins (do not invent — these are fixed by /essentials:init)

- **Package root**: `com.example.golden` (source `package` declarations and Maven coordinates derive from this)
- **Maven groupId / artifactId**: `com.example` / `golden`
- **Stack version pins** (Spring Boot, the language and Java levels, Trustworks Essentials, and every other dependency): authoritative in `golden/pom.xml`'s `<properties>` and `golden/frontend/package.json`. Read them before any planning step that names a dependency, version, or language level. Do **not** propose your own pins, do **not** "upgrade to latest", and do **not** invent versions that look plausible.

## Code locations for new code

- Backend (production): `golden/backend/src/main/java/com/example/golden/...`
- Backend (tests): `golden/backend/src/test/java/com/example/golden/...`
- Backend resources / config: `golden/backend/src/main/resources/`
- Frontend (production): `golden/frontend/src/...`
- Frontend (tests): co-located with the source they test (`*.test.ts` / `*.test.tsx`), run by vitest
- Generated API client (do not hand-edit): `golden/frontend/src/shared/api/generated/`
- OpenAPI contract (regenerated, not hand-edited): `golden/contracts/openapi.json`

## More

For full project context, framework-knowledge auto-loading (the `essentials-docs` skill), conventions, and commands, see **`golden/CLAUDE.md`** — that file is the project-level source of truth.
